-- X21 (SHADOW-SEMANTICS S1-PRELUDE (b), the boundary on the recovery spelling) -- #2640.
--
-- x19 makes every prelude binding a module can NAME reachable as `C.<name>`.  The set that
-- licenses is core's EXPORT surface, computed the same way an ordinary module's is, and not
-- core's whole top-level namespace.  Without this cell the alias spelling would be free to
-- widen silently to every private core helper, and nothing in x19 could tell.
--
--   PINNED: located REJECT on check, run and build.  `indexGo` is a top-level binding of
--     `stdlib/core.mdk` that carries no `export`, so it is not in the alias surface.
--   The positive control rides in the diagnostic: the message suggests `C.index`, the
--     EXPORTED sibling, which is reachable.  A regression that widened the surface would
--     turn this cell green while leaving every other x-cell untouched.
--
-- #2640 asks a DIFFERENT question -- whether `check` should bind a private core helper under
-- its BARE name, which it does today -- and this cell neither answers nor depends on it.
-- The alias surface is narrower than the bare one on purpose, and stays narrower whichever
-- way #2640 is ruled.
import core as C

main = println (C.indexGo 0 [1, 2] 0)
